ese observations by fiscal year, where each fiscal year runs from July through June.\n\nFor FY1990 (July 1989 through June 1990), the 12 months are: July 1989 (2,824,487), Aug 1989 (2,860,454), Sept 1989 (2,881,112), Oct 1989 (2,924,765), Nov 1989 (2,946,111), Dec 1989 (2,975,537), Jan 1990 (2,996,900), Feb 1990 (3,025,827), Mar 1990 (3,081,893), Apr 1990 (3,093,076), and May 1990 (3,127,229).\n\nI need to sum these twelve monthly values to get the annual total.\n\nSimilarly, FY1991 covers July 1990 through June 1991 with monthly balances starting from 3,200,338 in July 1990 and progressing through 3,562,942 by June 1991. FY1992 spans July 1991 to June 1992, beginning with 3,597,294 in July 1991. FY1993 runs from July 1992 through June 1993, starting at 4,025,949 in July 1992. Once I have all the sums, I can calculate the regression and determine the projection.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_7f52fa8d157c41dca790595b","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport statistics\n\n# Monthly total federal securities outstanding (in millions) from July 1989 through June 1993\n# From the Treasury Bulletin data\n\n# FY1990: July 1989 - June 1990\nfy1990 = [\n    2824487,  # July 1989\n    2860454,  # Aug 1989\n    2881112,  # Sept 1989\n    2924765,  # Oct 1989\n    2946111,  # Nov 1989\n    2975537,  # Dec 1989\n    2996900,  # Jan 1990\n    3025827,  # Feb 1990\n    3081893,  # Mar 1990\n    3093076,  # Apr 1990\n    3127229,  # May 1990\n    3175461,  # June 1990\n]\n\n# FY1991: July 1990 - June 1991\nfy1991 = [\n    3200338,  # July 1990\n    3243281,  # Aug 1990\n    3266073,  # Sept 1990\n    3307748,  # Oct 1990\n    3363205,  # Nov 1990\n    3397325,  # Dec 1990\n    3443129,  # Jan 1991\n    3488624,  # Feb 1991\n    3491694,  # Mar 1991\n    3470530,  # Apr 1991\n    3522261,  # May 1991\n    3562942,  # June 1991\n]\n\n# FY1992: July 1991 - June 1992\nfy1992 = [\n    3597294,  # July 1991\n    3636298,  # Aug 1991\n    3683054,  # Sept 1991\n    3735584,  # Oct 1991\n    3766152,  # Nov 1991\n    3820403,  # Dec 1991\n    3826612,  # Jan 1992\n    3844741,  # Feb 1992\n    3897204,  # Mar 1992\n    3907963,  # Apr 1992\n    3950469,  # May 1992\n    4000678,  # June 1992\n]\n\n# FY1993: July 1992 - June 1993\nfy1993 = [\n    4025949,  # July 1992\n    4064327,  # Aug 1992\n    4082871,  # Sept 1992\n    4085732,  # Oct 1992\n    4151504,  # Nov 1992\n    4195926,  # Dec 1992\n    4185886,  # Jan 1993\n    4216166,  # Feb 1993\n    4250287,  # Mar 1993\n    4274361,  # Apr 1993\n    4316774,  # May 1993\n    4372677,  # June 1993\n]\n\n# Calculate sums for each fiscal year\nsum_fy1990 = sum(fy1990)\nsum_fy1991 = sum(fy1991)\nsum_fy1992 = sum(fy1992)\nsum_fy1993 = sum(fy1993)\n\nprint(f\"FY1990 sum: {sum_fy1990}\")\nprint(f\"FY1991 sum: {sum_fy1991}\")\nprint(f\"FY1992 sum: {sum_fy1992}\")\nprint(f\"FY1993 sum: {sum_fy1993}\")\n\n# Data for linear regression: fiscal year (x) vs sum (y)\nx = [1990, 1991, 1992, 1993]\ny = [sum_fy1990, sum_fy1991, sum_fy1992, sum_fy1993]\n\nprint(f\"\\nData points:\")\nfor xi, yi in zip(x, y):\n    print(f\"  FY{xi}: {yi:,}\")\n\n# Calculate linear regression\nn = len(x)\nsum_x = sum(x)\nsum_y = sum(y)\nsum_xy = sum(xi * yi for xi, yi in zip(x, y))\nsum_x2 = sum(xi ** 2 for xi in x)\n\n# Slope (m) and intercept (b)\nm = (n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y) / (n * sum_x2 - sum_x ** 2)\nb = (sum_y - m * sum_x) / n\n\nprint(f\"\\nLinear regression:\")\nprint(f\"  Slope (m): {m}\")\nprint(f\"  Intercept (b): {b}\")\nprint(f\"  Equation: y = {m}x + {b}\")\n\n# Project for FY1995\nx_1995 = 1995\ny_1995 = m * x_1995 + b\navg_1995 = y_1995 / 12\n\nprint(f\"\\nProjection for FY1995:\")\nprint(f\"  Sum: {y_1995:,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"  Average (sum/12): {avg_1995:,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"  Rounded: {round(avg_1995)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
